Description: High-performance version bumper CLI written in Rust
 bump2version (bump) is a fully compatible, Rust-native reimplementation of
 bumpversion/bump-my-version. It manages version numbers across any file type,
 creates git commits and tags, and supports Cargo workspaces, pre-release
 cycling, watch mode, and multi-language manifest auto-detection.
 .
 Features include:
  * Increments major, minor, patch, or any custom version component
  * Multi-line search/replace patterns
  * Cargo workspace atomic bumping
  * Watch mode for automated bumping on save
  * Multi-language auto-detection (Rust, Python, JS, Go, Java, Ruby)
  * Usable as cargo subcommand: cargo bump
